            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for a baby shower, then the Tamil for a housewarming."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: மணமுடி",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மணமுடி — maṇamuṭi — \"to wed; to marry\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "அவர் கடந்த ஆண்டு ஒரு ஆசிரியையை மணமுடித்தார். avar kaṭanta āṇṭu oru āciriyaiyai maṇamuṭittār. Last year he married a teacher."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): மணமுடித்தேன், maṇamuṭittēṉ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A written word for திருமணம் செய்; the spouse takes -ஐ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மணமுடி (maṇamuṭi) is a Tamil compound built from மணம், \"union, marriage\" (DEDR 4667), and முடி, \"to tie, fasten\" (DEDR 4921)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
